{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And he ran toward him.</b> For he thought he was bringing money, seeing that the servant of the house came here with ten laden camels." "<b>And he embraced him.</b> When he saw nothing with him, he said: perhaps he brought gold pieces and they are in his lap." "<b>And he kissed him.</b> He said: perhaps he brought pearls and they are in his mouth. Bereshit Rabbah." "<b>And he told Lavan.</b> That he came only because of his brother's coercion, and that they took his money from him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:05.006510881Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}